FIGURE-IDENTITY PROOF — ADR-026 Amendment 2 clause (b)
==============================================================================

WHAT THIS PROVES, AND WHY IT EXISTS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADR-026 §5 permits ONE re-measurement and forbids touching the harness afterwards.
Amendment 2 clarifies that the rule binds measurement-affecting code, not
presentation prose — but only if the prose fix ships a proof that no measured
number moved, because the judgment that a change 'provably cannot' move a figure
is never the executor's alone. This file is that proof, committed so a reviewer
can CHECK it rather than take it on trust (clause (c)).

  pre-fix  report: generated at code commit 7c8261d7a834 (the single §5 run)
  post-fix report: generated at code commit fbcfcf593552 (prose fix only)
  change under proof: eval/run_all.py `numeric_claims` DetectorUnderTest.note

The `note` field is read at run_all.py:286 (copied into DetectorResult) and
:385-386 (rendered to markdown). It is on no scoring path. That is the structural
claim; everything below is the empirical check of it.

